1
00:00:11,063 --> 00:00:15,943
INTERSPECIES EXCHANGE

2
00:00:16,026 --> 00:00:17,486
MADARA-GUMI

3
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:19,530
[screams, groans]

4
00:00:22,742 --> 00:00:25,453
- [groans]
- [Melon chuckles]

5
00:00:26,537 --> 00:00:29,832
The thing is,
I can't stand those spots of yours...

6
00:00:29,915 --> 00:00:31,792
- [explosion]
- [grunts]

7
00:00:34,253 --> 00:00:36,422
The Doku-Gumi wanna play.

8
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:42,511
[Savon] You fought well, boy.

9
00:00:42,595 --> 00:00:44,054
Color me "impressed".

10
00:00:45,181 --> 00:00:46,974
On behalf of the Doku-Gumi...

11
00:00:47,516 --> 00:00:50,186
it wasn't our intention
to put you six feet under.

12
00:00:51,353 --> 00:00:52,313
I have to say,

13
00:00:52,396 --> 00:00:55,316
we aren't exactly "fan favorites"
around these parts.

14
00:00:55,816 --> 00:00:58,069
And I'm getting tired of that.

15
00:00:58,152 --> 00:01:02,281
So now, it's out with the discrimination
and in with the triumph.

16
00:01:02,364 --> 00:01:04,742
Everyone's gonna see how special we are.

17
00:01:04,825 --> 00:01:07,328
You're supposed to respect the Doku-Gumi...

18
00:01:07,411 --> 00:01:08,746
- [rocks rumble]
- [sighs]

19
00:01:10,414 --> 00:01:12,166
[Legoshi groans softly]

20
00:01:13,084 --> 00:01:15,252
[Legoshi strains]

21
00:01:15,336 --> 00:01:17,171
[panting]

22
00:01:18,631 --> 00:01:20,299
[Legoshi] "A freshly severed limb

23
00:01:20,382 --> 00:01:22,301
still has some life", right?

24
00:01:24,011 --> 00:01:26,514
I'd feel sorry for it
if I let it get injured...

25
00:01:27,431 --> 00:01:28,641
{\an8}You're tellin' me

26
00:01:29,141 --> 00:01:30,476
{\an8}you took that blast...

27
00:01:30,976 --> 00:01:33,187
<i>just to protect that piece of tail?</i>

28
00:01:34,939 --> 00:01:37,316
I kinda panicked
and shoved it in my underwear,

29
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:39,068
I hope you don't take any offense.

30
00:01:42,196 --> 00:01:44,490
A tail that's been cut off
can't be reattached.

31
00:01:45,116 --> 00:01:46,784
The pride of the Doku-Gumi...

32
00:01:47,535 --> 00:01:48,828
I entrust it to you.

33
00:01:48,911 --> 00:01:49,954
[sighs]

34
00:01:58,921 --> 00:01:59,880
[Ten] Yoo hoo!

35
00:02:00,756 --> 00:02:01,590
[gasps]

36
00:02:02,508 --> 00:02:04,593
You're pretty good for a little wolf cub.

37
00:02:04,677 --> 00:02:07,596
[groans] <i>Oh, don't tell me.
Now I have to fight a girl?</i>

38
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,515
[Ten] All a woman has to do is touch you

39
00:02:09,598 --> 00:02:12,184
and look at how your tail
stands straight up.

40
00:02:12,726 --> 00:02:16,188
[gasps] Men really are
the simplest creatures, huh?

41
00:02:16,272 --> 00:02:18,566
Any elegance you see in the Black Market

42
00:02:18,649 --> 00:02:21,777
is going to be because of the Inari-Gumi.

43
00:02:21,861 --> 00:02:26,157
Kind of like the charming seductress
your little tail can't seem to resist!

44
00:02:26,824 --> 00:02:28,909
[Ten laughing]

45
00:02:34,582 --> 00:02:37,042
[indistinct conversation]

46
00:02:37,585 --> 00:02:38,752
{\an8}[scoffs]

47
00:02:38,836 --> 00:02:40,504
FESTIVAL SCHEDULE

48
00:02:40,588 --> 00:02:42,423
3. SURPRISE ANNOUNCEMENT (FOOD)

49
00:02:42,506 --> 00:02:46,385
[Mayor] <i>This meat was artificially created
through the wonders of science.</i>

50
00:02:46,468 --> 00:02:49,930
Meaning, no one died
for this meat to exist.

51
00:02:50,014 --> 00:02:52,433
And it can be consumed ethically.

52
00:02:52,516 --> 00:02:56,604
{\an8}The lab results show,
the cultured meat wasn't fully lab-grown,

53
00:02:56,687 --> 00:02:59,523
{\an8}it was partly made from fetal embryos.

54
00:02:59,607 --> 00:03:02,276
The mayor, he investigated
the relationship

55
00:03:02,359 --> 00:03:03,777
between you and your father,

56
00:03:03,861 --> 00:03:06,572
and it seems he has some kind of evidence.

57
00:03:07,323 --> 00:03:09,199
[sighs] <i>It'll be fine.</i>

58
00:03:09,283 --> 00:03:10,367
<i>I can do this.</i>

59
00:03:12,453 --> 00:03:14,622
[both grunting]

60
00:03:21,462 --> 00:03:23,005
[both grunting, groaning]

61
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:25,424
- [Ten groans]
- [Legoshi exclaims in pain]

62
00:03:25,925 --> 00:03:27,968
You going easy on me because I'm a girl?

63
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:30,930
If that's why you lose then that's on you.

64
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:33,682
Just remember, it wasn't me
who told you to do that.

65
00:03:34,683 --> 00:03:36,644
Y'know, everyone always says,

66
00:03:36,727 --> 00:03:38,896
female foxes are wicked creatures

67
00:03:38,979 --> 00:03:41,357
who trick people
using their seductive charm.

68
00:03:42,191 --> 00:03:43,734
I'm over that stereotype.

69
00:03:44,235 --> 00:03:46,237
I want to win, grow stronger,

70
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,197
and prove them all wrong.

71
00:03:48,739 --> 00:03:50,241
That's my sole focus.

72
00:03:50,783 --> 00:03:51,951
[Legoshi] Yeah I get it.

73
00:03:53,452 --> 00:03:54,578
Same for wolves.

74
00:03:55,246 --> 00:03:57,414
No one really seems to understand us.

75
00:03:57,957 --> 00:03:59,291
[sighs]

76
00:03:59,375 --> 00:04:01,835
You see it in books and movies
all the time:

77
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:03,879
the wolf is the bad guy.

78
00:04:03,963 --> 00:04:05,798
And it follows me around everywhere.

79
00:04:05,881 --> 00:04:07,007
So I get it.

80
00:04:07,091 --> 00:04:08,634
Is that right?

81
00:04:08,717 --> 00:04:10,469
You're bold and insightful...

82
00:04:11,262 --> 00:04:13,180
Still, doesn't mean you get mercy!

83
00:04:13,806 --> 00:04:16,767
- [Ten groans]
- [Legoshi groans]

84
00:04:20,312 --> 00:04:21,230
[yelps]

85
00:04:22,231 --> 00:04:23,816
[panting]

86
00:04:23,899 --> 00:04:26,694
{\an8}It felt like you two
were taking your sweet time...

87
00:04:26,777 --> 00:04:29,947
{\an8}Apologies for giving into my impatience...

88
00:04:30,948 --> 00:04:33,409
{\an8}ONLY COMPANY RESEARCHERS BEYOND THIS POINT

89
00:04:39,123 --> 00:04:41,250
<i>I don't even know why I'm doing this.</i>

90
00:04:44,211 --> 00:04:45,045
[sighs]

91
00:04:46,005 --> 00:04:46,964
<i>Here it is.</i>

92
00:04:53,721 --> 00:04:55,264
Is that a live stream?

93
00:04:55,347 --> 00:04:56,432
[Miguno] Yeah.

94
00:04:57,099 --> 00:04:58,017
Check it out.

95
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,435
It's from the Black Market.

96
00:04:59,518 --> 00:05:02,062
[Durham] The Black Market?
They're not allowed to show that.

97
00:05:02,146 --> 00:05:03,856
Ough, he's covered in blood!

98
00:05:04,523 --> 00:05:06,984
{\an8}[exclaims in surprise] Is that...
It's Legoshi!

99
00:05:07,067 --> 00:05:08,777
{\an8}- [Durham] No way!
- [Miguno] That's crazy!

100
00:05:08,861 --> 00:05:10,696
{\an8}[crowd cheering]

101
00:05:10,779 --> 00:05:11,947
{\an8}[Mayor] The Zoolympics!

102
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:15,409
A world class competition involving...

103
00:05:15,492 --> 00:05:19,371
some of the most talented
and skilled athletes on the planet.

104
00:05:20,539 --> 00:05:22,708
Regardless of species,

105
00:05:22,791 --> 00:05:24,835
of age, or of gender,

106
00:05:24,918 --> 00:05:26,837
this event inspires all of us,

107
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:30,049
to strive for co-existence and prosperity.

108
00:05:33,719 --> 00:05:37,056
However, before we can host the games,

109
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:40,350
our city needs to overcome some challenges
such as...

110
00:05:40,434 --> 00:05:41,685
infrastructure,

111
00:05:41,769 --> 00:05:44,563
devouring incidents
and construction delays.

112
00:05:45,606 --> 00:05:46,648
In light of that,

113
00:05:46,732 --> 00:05:49,526
we do have a major announcement
to share with you all!

114
00:05:50,694 --> 00:05:51,653
Here it is.

115
00:05:53,030 --> 00:05:55,991
- [male 1] Can they talk about that?
- [male 2] They finally admit it exists?

116
00:05:56,075 --> 00:05:58,994
- [male 3] Oh, you know this is bad.
- [indistinct chatter]

117
00:05:59,078 --> 00:06:00,496
NEW STADIUM BUILDING

118
00:06:00,579 --> 00:06:02,456
[Louis] <i>"Demolition of the Black Market"?</i>

119
00:06:04,083 --> 00:06:05,793
<i>This isn't in the script!</i>

120
00:06:05,876 --> 00:06:07,961
[sighs] They set me up!

121
00:06:08,045 --> 00:06:09,338
[Mayor] Quiet please!

122
00:06:09,421 --> 00:06:10,506
Just settle down!

123
00:06:11,507 --> 00:06:13,967
I know the Black Market is controversial.

124
00:06:14,051 --> 00:06:15,761
Some say it's a necessity.

125
00:06:15,844 --> 00:06:18,305
It acts as a safe haven for carnivores.

126
00:06:18,847 --> 00:06:21,225
So they can satisfy their desire for meat.

127
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:25,562
Unfortunately, the Black Market
represents something much darker.

128
00:06:26,188 --> 00:06:28,649
It's currently sheltering
a dangerous criminal.

129
00:06:29,358 --> 00:06:33,821
Our sources tell us the gray wolf Legoshi,
is hiding out in the Market

130
00:06:33,904 --> 00:06:34,738
[groans]

131
00:06:34,822 --> 00:06:36,824
- So they found him?
- Well, it's about time.

132
00:06:39,368 --> 00:06:40,327
Oh, Legoshi...

133
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:45,374
But fear not. We'll bring you news
of his arrest very soon.

134
00:06:45,457 --> 00:06:47,876
- [crowd cheering]
- Right, my friend?

135
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:48,794
Right.

136
00:06:48,877 --> 00:06:50,546
[applause]

137
00:06:52,047 --> 00:06:54,716
[drums beating]

138
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:58,262
[tribal music playing]

139
00:07:04,268 --> 00:07:06,270
[Melon grunting]

140
00:07:10,983 --> 00:07:13,277
A beautiful red flower!

141
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:16,196
The first of many
that will bloom in my fields!

142
00:07:16,989 --> 00:07:20,075
You can plant your flowers,
and they may bloom...

143
00:07:20,784 --> 00:07:22,911
But it's pointless
if they don't bear fruit!

144
00:07:22,995 --> 00:07:25,372
[both grunting]

145
00:07:25,456 --> 00:07:26,540
[laughs maniacally]]

146
00:07:26,623 --> 00:07:27,749
Finally!

147
00:07:27,833 --> 00:07:31,003
Now you're getting it!
That's what I want to see!

148
00:07:31,086 --> 00:07:33,005
[both grunting]

149
00:07:34,465 --> 00:07:35,799
- [grunts]
- [groans]

150
00:07:36,341 --> 00:07:38,260
[groaning in pain]

151
00:07:39,470 --> 00:07:41,430
[Melon] Not trying to run away, are you?

152
00:07:42,097 --> 00:07:44,057
[grunts]

153
00:07:45,309 --> 00:07:47,561
When people run, I can't help but chase!

154
00:07:48,228 --> 00:07:52,191
You can thank my leopard mom
for my hunting instincts.

155
00:07:52,274 --> 00:07:54,026
[Legoshi] <i>I won't be able to hold him off.</i>

156
00:07:54,109 --> 00:07:55,652
<i>Melon will keep getting stronger,</i>

157
00:07:55,736 --> 00:07:57,029
<i>and I'll run out of steam.</i>

158
00:07:57,905 --> 00:07:58,822
[grunts]

159
00:08:00,657 --> 00:08:04,161
You've gotta tell me
how it feels to be the prey for once...

160
00:08:04,244 --> 00:08:06,663
[thuds, straining]

161
00:08:06,747 --> 00:08:10,125
{\an8}I'm guessing that's a terror
you've never felt...

162
00:08:10,209 --> 00:08:12,377
[gurgling]

163
00:08:14,087 --> 00:08:15,881
[gasping]

164
00:08:23,847 --> 00:08:26,934
[Legoshi] <i>My dark self was always there
inside of me.</i>

165
00:08:28,018 --> 00:08:31,980
<i>With his hands...
he could take any life he wanted...</i>

166
00:08:33,482 --> 00:08:37,694
<i>All the worries I had about
my relationships with herbivores...</i>

167
00:08:37,778 --> 00:08:40,614
<i>But those worries were so insignificant,</i>

168
00:08:40,697 --> 00:08:45,577
<i>compared to the fear
felt by those who might be preyed upon.</i>

169
00:08:46,411 --> 00:08:47,454
<i>I am...</i>

170
00:08:48,705 --> 00:08:49,998
<i>I...</i>

171
00:08:50,082 --> 00:08:51,166
<i>am...</i>

172
00:08:51,250 --> 00:08:56,338
[wolf howls]

173
00:08:58,674 --> 00:09:02,803
[dogs howling]

174
00:09:03,345 --> 00:09:07,349
[howling intensifies]

175
00:09:14,606 --> 00:09:21,405
[all howl]

176
00:09:31,164 --> 00:09:32,541
[Legoshi] <i>It's them.</i>

177
00:09:38,130 --> 00:09:39,464
- Huh?
- [thud]

178
00:09:41,383 --> 00:09:46,555
[howling]

179
00:09:46,638 --> 00:09:48,974
- That's gotta be Legoshi!
- [giggles]

180
00:09:49,933 --> 00:09:54,229
[all howling]

181
00:09:55,147 --> 00:09:57,691
- [thud]
- [Legoshi groans]

182
00:10:00,402 --> 00:10:01,695
[Melon growls]

183
00:10:01,778 --> 00:10:04,197
[grunting]

184
00:10:05,115 --> 00:10:05,949
[Louis] <i>Legoshi,</i>

185
00:10:06,533 --> 00:10:08,535
<i>you're really giving it your all.</i>

186
00:10:09,036 --> 00:10:10,912
<i>Your pain and suffering though...</i>

187
00:10:12,122 --> 00:10:14,791
<i>It's not less painful
just because you share it.</i>

188
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:17,127
<i>I know what I must do...</i>

189
00:10:17,210 --> 00:10:19,296
<i>if both of us carry
our share of the burden</i>

190
00:10:19,379 --> 00:10:20,922
<i>our strength will grow...</i>

191
00:10:25,594 --> 00:10:27,346
[Melon growls, chuckles]

192
00:10:29,931 --> 00:10:31,266
[drums beating]

193
00:10:39,816 --> 00:10:41,485
[both grunting]

194
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:46,448
- [Legoshi sighs in pain]
- [Melon grunts]

195
00:10:48,533 --> 00:10:50,327
[Melon woos, chuckles]

196
00:10:50,410 --> 00:10:53,038
[Melon] Admit it,
you're having a great time.

197
00:10:53,121 --> 00:10:57,793
The mess. The gore. The pain...
makes you feel alive, doesn't it?

198
00:10:59,002 --> 00:11:00,337
[laugh]

199
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:03,048
Ever notice,
hatred works both ways.

200
00:11:03,131 --> 00:11:04,633
It's mutually beneficial.

201
00:11:04,716 --> 00:11:08,637
When I show you my hatred,
you return that hate back to me.

202
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:11,765
Giving both of us
that precious will to live.

203
00:11:13,475 --> 00:11:15,519
Exposing new parts of us,

204
00:11:15,602 --> 00:11:17,896
parts that were just wasting away...

205
00:11:17,979 --> 00:11:21,733
But it all wakes up as you and I
try to rip each other's throats out.

206
00:11:22,317 --> 00:11:23,693
- [Legoshi grunts]
- [Melon chuckles]

207
00:11:23,777 --> 00:11:26,822
There's nothing "lukewarm"
about this romance.

208
00:11:26,905 --> 00:11:29,950
What we're experiencing right now
is true love!

209
00:11:30,033 --> 00:11:31,326
[Legoshi screaming]

210
00:11:39,251 --> 00:11:42,587
[Melon gasping]

211
00:11:51,138 --> 00:11:53,014
[Melon chuckles, pants]

212
00:12:12,117 --> 00:12:13,785
[chuckles]

213
00:12:13,869 --> 00:12:16,079
I'm so getting fired for this.

214
00:12:19,291 --> 00:12:20,876
[gasping]

215
00:12:26,131 --> 00:12:27,215
[Legoshi] Melon?

216
00:12:29,968 --> 00:12:31,678
Nice...

217
00:12:31,761 --> 00:12:34,681
The experiment is working
just as I predicted.

218
00:12:35,682 --> 00:12:38,185
We're witnessing the weakness of a hybrid.

219
00:12:38,268 --> 00:12:42,147
He's reacting to the scent created
when carnivore and herbivore blood mixes.

220
00:12:43,106 --> 00:12:45,609
Judging from this, it's quite effective.

221
00:12:45,692 --> 00:12:47,986
[groans] I shouldn't have let you live.

222
00:12:48,945 --> 00:12:50,363
[footsteps approaching]

223
00:12:51,031 --> 00:12:53,200
This isn't a fight to the death.

224
00:12:53,283 --> 00:12:55,160
It's supposed to be a turf war.

225
00:12:56,244 --> 00:12:58,747
- And it's over.
- [Melon grunts]

226
00:12:59,581 --> 00:13:00,624
[Melon grunts]

227
00:13:02,209 --> 00:13:03,835
So what's next?

228
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:07,339
We all get cleaned up
and we're best friends? [laughs]

229
00:13:07,422 --> 00:13:10,383
You've got to be kidding me
with this nonsense.

230
00:13:11,009 --> 00:13:12,093
I know,

231
00:13:12,177 --> 00:13:14,513
why don't we have
a little picnic together?

232
00:13:14,596 --> 00:13:18,183
Foxes, tigers, and lizards,
all one happy family!

233
00:13:18,266 --> 00:13:20,101
We should hold hands.

234
00:13:20,727 --> 00:13:23,647
We'll just stop fighting
and leave the past in the past.

235
00:13:23,730 --> 00:13:25,398
[laughing]

236
00:13:25,482 --> 00:13:28,860
Now, let's raise a toast to our unity!

237
00:13:29,903 --> 00:13:32,531
You're nothing but a bunch of fakes.

238
00:13:32,614 --> 00:13:33,990
[Legoshi] I feel for you.

239
00:13:35,575 --> 00:13:36,451
You're lonely.

240
00:13:36,993 --> 00:13:40,372
Every interaction you've ever had
has been terrible for you.

241
00:13:41,581 --> 00:13:43,792
But actually you're not alone.

242
00:13:43,875 --> 00:13:45,710
I know exactly how you feel.

243
00:13:46,461 --> 00:13:47,379
All of us,

244
00:13:47,462 --> 00:13:49,631
searching for the right words
at the right time.

245
00:13:50,298 --> 00:13:52,926
We become absorbed in these conversations.

246
00:13:53,009 --> 00:13:54,761
If we learned to express ourselves...

247
00:13:54,844 --> 00:13:58,139
{\an8}- well then, someday--
- Just spare me the performance.

248
00:13:58,223 --> 00:14:00,267
I'm not the audience for your speech.

249
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,228
[all gasp]

250
00:14:03,311 --> 00:14:05,981
Let me go ahead and write the ending.

251
00:14:06,064 --> 00:14:08,608
When you think about
the great masterpieces,

252
00:14:08,692 --> 00:14:11,528
they always tend to end up in tragedy.

253
00:14:11,611 --> 00:14:13,446
[laughs]

254
00:14:13,530 --> 00:14:16,700
And this one's going to leave
a bad taste in your mouth...

255
00:14:16,783 --> 00:14:20,453
Imagine a mixed beast dying
in a place like this!

256
00:14:20,537 --> 00:14:22,414
- [all gasp]
- No!

257
00:14:22,497 --> 00:14:23,623
[gunshot]

258
00:14:32,090 --> 00:14:33,842
{\an8}Oh, no... Melon, why?

259
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,929
[groans]

260
00:14:38,013 --> 00:14:41,933
You should be more concerned about
someone else's life. [gasps for air]

261
00:14:42,017 --> 00:14:45,103
She's at
the Festival of the Meteor, right?

262
00:14:45,186 --> 00:14:48,356
- [female] Good work, Legoshi!
- [gasps softly]

263
00:14:49,149 --> 00:14:51,902
Oh, the despair I've prepared for you...

264
00:14:52,861 --> 00:14:55,655
I hope you savor every bit of it.

265
00:14:55,739 --> 00:14:57,198
Legoshi...

266
00:14:59,284 --> 00:15:01,119
Festival of the Meteor...

267
00:15:01,828 --> 00:15:03,371
He talkin' about the Melda?

268
00:15:04,372 --> 00:15:06,166
[Deshico] If it gets used at the venue...

269
00:15:07,417 --> 00:15:11,129
[Haru] <i>Let's go to the Festival Of
The Meteor, and light a candle together.</i>

270
00:15:11,212 --> 00:15:12,130
<i>Make a promise.</i>

271
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:14,382
Oh, no!

272
00:15:16,134 --> 00:15:18,136
Excuse me! Sorry!

273
00:15:18,219 --> 00:15:19,054
[male] Who won?

274
00:15:21,514 --> 00:15:22,474
<i>Haru...</i>

275
00:15:23,683 --> 00:15:25,393
[panting]

276
00:15:30,190 --> 00:15:31,858
C'mon, grandson! Get on!

277
00:15:31,942 --> 00:15:32,859
Grandpa!

278
00:15:33,401 --> 00:15:34,903
[bike revving]

279
00:15:42,702 --> 00:15:45,163
- [female] What is he saying?
- [male] You can't do that!

280
00:15:45,872 --> 00:15:48,541
Louis, is your leg bothering you?

281
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:49,793
Oh, no.

282
00:15:49,876 --> 00:15:52,712
- It's not a problem.
- Well, then, keep going...

283
00:15:54,255 --> 00:15:57,550
[Louis] <i>Earlier today, we announced
the demolition of the Black Market.</i>

284
00:15:58,510 --> 00:15:59,678
I ask,

285
00:15:59,761 --> 00:16:02,263
to every carnivore that is here tonight.

286
00:16:02,347 --> 00:16:04,432
Is that something you're all okay with?

287
00:16:04,933 --> 00:16:06,309
Uh...

288
00:16:06,393 --> 00:16:08,186
I see your fangs are yellow.

289
00:16:08,269 --> 00:16:10,939
I'm guessing
you love eating horse meat, right?

290
00:16:11,439 --> 00:16:13,024
I see you sweat a lot.

291
00:16:13,108 --> 00:16:16,152
You probably eat a lot of oily organ meat.

292
00:16:16,695 --> 00:16:18,738
<i>Why is he going off script?!</i>

293
00:16:19,447 --> 00:16:20,865
I ask you.

294
00:16:20,949 --> 00:16:23,159
Can we really blame them for their nature?

295
00:16:23,827 --> 00:16:25,412
Sometimes we laugh together,

296
00:16:25,495 --> 00:16:26,955
and sometimes we cry.

297
00:16:27,038 --> 00:16:29,457
But when we see the fangs in their mouths,

298
00:16:29,541 --> 00:16:31,626
we can't help but have a reaction.

299
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,462
The truth is
carnivores are going to eat meat.

300
00:16:34,546 --> 00:16:36,047
That's just a simple fact of life.

301
00:16:37,424 --> 00:16:39,092
[male 4] This is making me uncomfortable.

302
00:16:39,175 --> 00:16:41,553
[Louis] Herbivores and carnivores
should interact.

303
00:16:41,636 --> 00:16:43,138
{\an8}<i>That's the only way forward.</i>

304
00:16:43,221 --> 00:16:45,890
{\an8}[female reporter] <i>This has definitely
taken an unexpected turn.</i>

305
00:16:46,850 --> 00:16:49,185
[Riz] At least Louis is keeping them
on their toes.

306
00:16:49,769 --> 00:16:52,147
<i>Well, maybe the world won't really change</i>

307
00:16:52,230 --> 00:16:55,108
<i>unless someone shines
a light on these things.</i>

308
00:16:55,191 --> 00:16:56,484
Good to see you and all, but...

309
00:16:56,568 --> 00:16:58,611
don't you have a performance to get to?

310
00:16:59,154 --> 00:17:02,407
You know what, Riz, I really wanted you
to see the play live.

311
00:17:03,199 --> 00:17:04,242
Oh yeah?

312
00:17:04,325 --> 00:17:06,703
You were my first guy friend after all.

313
00:17:07,245 --> 00:17:08,204
[gasp]

314
00:17:11,708 --> 00:17:12,876
Thank you for that.

315
00:17:13,793 --> 00:17:17,922
It's perfectly natural that
herbivores would be worried about this.

316
00:17:18,006 --> 00:17:21,885
That's why,
we have prepared a revolutionary solution.

317
00:17:23,344 --> 00:17:25,972
Okay, talk about the artificial meat.

318
00:17:26,056 --> 00:17:27,015
Got it.

319
00:17:31,895 --> 00:17:32,937
<i>Ibuki,</i>

320
00:17:33,605 --> 00:17:35,815
<i>in the end your greatest sin,</i>

321
00:17:35,899 --> 00:17:39,027
<i>might have been turning me
into a wild buck.</i>

322
00:17:42,155 --> 00:17:43,323
The Black Market...

323
00:17:44,074 --> 00:17:45,116
Is my home.

324
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,868
I was product ID number 4.

325
00:17:46,951 --> 00:17:48,661
[all stunned]

326
00:17:49,454 --> 00:17:51,164
I was a powerless young kid.

327
00:17:51,247 --> 00:17:52,415
Born in a cage.

328
00:17:52,499 --> 00:17:55,043
I was supposed to be sold
in the Black Market as meat.

329
00:17:55,126 --> 00:17:56,252
[crowd gasps]

330
00:17:57,337 --> 00:17:58,421
Is that the truth?

331
00:18:01,341 --> 00:18:03,176
Chairman Ogma purchased me,

332
00:18:03,676 --> 00:18:06,387
and raised me as heir
to The Horns Conglomerate.

333
00:18:06,888 --> 00:18:08,515
He treated me like his own son.

334
00:18:11,184 --> 00:18:13,728
Someone found out about my origins

335
00:18:13,812 --> 00:18:15,522
and threatened my father with it.

336
00:18:16,314 --> 00:18:17,315
That person

337
00:18:18,024 --> 00:18:19,109
is the mayor!

338
00:18:19,859 --> 00:18:21,820
What? Louis, what are you doing?

339
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:23,404
It's the truth.

340
00:18:23,488 --> 00:18:26,783
The mayor tried to blackmail
an enormous bribe out of my father.

341
00:18:26,866 --> 00:18:30,036
[chuckles nervously]
I have no idea what he's talking about...

342
00:18:30,787 --> 00:18:31,830
Right, father?

343
00:18:31,913 --> 00:18:33,540
[growling]

344
00:18:34,582 --> 00:18:35,583
Um-hmm.

345
00:18:35,667 --> 00:18:37,627
What do you have to say for yourself,
Mr. Mayor?

346
00:18:37,710 --> 00:18:39,796
- Is all this true?
- Fake news.

347
00:18:40,588 --> 00:18:42,173
[Louis] And he didn't stop there.

348
00:18:42,257 --> 00:18:44,926
He extorted money
from the Zoolympics sponsors, too.

349
00:18:45,844 --> 00:18:48,513
This Zoolympic bid is full of dirty money.

350
00:18:49,472 --> 00:18:52,350
Wake up! Don't fall for his lies!

351
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:53,601
He's a disgrace.

352
00:18:53,685 --> 00:18:56,146
Bringing dishonor to the kings of beasts!

353
00:18:56,646 --> 00:18:57,647
Huh?

354
00:18:57,730 --> 00:18:59,607
[grunting]

355
00:19:04,237 --> 00:19:05,947
[roars]

356
00:19:06,573 --> 00:19:09,033
[crowd screams]

357
00:19:14,831 --> 00:19:16,207
[grunts]

358
00:19:16,291 --> 00:19:17,500
[growls]

359
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:23,548
Legoshi...

360
00:19:24,591 --> 00:19:28,469
[both grunting]

361
00:19:42,650 --> 00:19:45,403
- [male 5] He's-- He's the devourer!
- [male 6] Someone stop him!

362
00:19:45,486 --> 00:19:47,447
- [male 7] Run away!
- [female] Don't look, Sweetie!

363
00:19:47,530 --> 00:19:49,699
- [male 8] Stay back!
- [male 9] Where are the police?

364
00:19:53,161 --> 00:19:53,995
[strains]

365
00:19:57,373 --> 00:19:59,834
- [male 8] Let's get outta here.
- [male 9] I don't want to die!

366
00:19:59,918 --> 00:20:00,960
[male 5] He might eat us!

367
00:20:01,044 --> 00:20:03,421
[male 4] That's the devourer
from the news!

368
00:20:04,505 --> 00:20:06,382
He's not a devourer!

369
00:20:07,133 --> 00:20:08,218
You're wrong!

370
00:20:09,052 --> 00:20:10,386
He's just Legoshi...

371
00:20:10,887 --> 00:20:12,805
He'd never do something like that!

372
00:20:17,936 --> 00:20:19,812
Wow, I don't think I'd be that brave.

373
00:20:23,775 --> 00:20:25,026
Oh, Legoshi...

374
00:20:28,905 --> 00:20:29,822
Haru...

375
00:20:29,906 --> 00:20:31,741
You're alright.

376
00:20:32,367 --> 00:20:34,994
Yeah. Did you close your eyes?

377
00:20:36,204 --> 00:20:37,830
I was looking at you.

378
00:20:37,914 --> 00:20:39,832
They should be closed when we kiss!

379
00:20:40,708 --> 00:20:41,626
Wanna try again?

380
00:20:45,755 --> 00:20:46,881
Go, Legoshi...

381
00:20:49,968 --> 00:20:51,219
[Haru chuckles softly]

382
00:20:52,470 --> 00:20:56,391
[Yahya] That gray wolf was framed,
he's no devourer.

383
00:20:56,474 --> 00:20:57,558
He's innocent.

384
00:20:57,642 --> 00:20:59,560
I admire his bravery.

385
00:20:59,644 --> 00:21:02,563
He sought justice
in spite of being accused.

386
00:21:02,647 --> 00:21:05,858
He didn't stop until
he captured the actual criminal.

387
00:21:06,442 --> 00:21:07,277
Legoshi...

388
00:21:08,278 --> 00:21:10,029
really well done.

389
00:21:10,113 --> 00:21:11,322
Mr. Yahya...

390
00:21:12,907 --> 00:21:15,576
[applause]

391
00:21:16,869 --> 00:21:18,329
I do apologize, Father.

392
00:21:18,413 --> 00:21:19,455
But I had to.

393
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:22,625
This is the path I've chosen for myself.

394
00:21:23,793 --> 00:21:25,962
Well sometimes our plans...

395
00:21:26,045 --> 00:21:27,797
don't go the way we want.

396
00:21:28,881 --> 00:21:30,091
Your prosthetic leg

397
00:21:30,758 --> 00:21:33,428
will climb so much higher
than I ever could.

398
00:21:38,057 --> 00:21:39,809
Looks like they really did it.

399
00:21:39,892 --> 00:21:40,727
You're right.

400
00:21:41,519 --> 00:21:44,355
These kids are more than one
single Beastar.

401
00:21:44,939 --> 00:21:47,317
Yeah, they're Beastars.

402
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,234
Right.

403
00:21:49,944 --> 00:21:51,112
[crowd cheering]

404
00:22:00,163 --> 00:22:02,248
{\an8}[theme song playing]

405
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,754
[voiceover] <i>The drama club
put on their play</i>

406
00:22:07,837 --> 00:22:09,630
<i>shortly after the real life drama</i>

407
00:22:09,714 --> 00:22:11,591
<i>and it was a huge success.</i>

408
00:22:12,425 --> 00:22:15,636
<i>The mayor was arrested
on multiple bribery charges.</i>

409
00:22:16,471 --> 00:22:18,056
<i>And those weren't the only crimes.</i>

410
00:22:18,139 --> 00:22:20,933
<i>Turns out there was blackmail
and intimidation, too.</i>

411
00:22:21,601 --> 00:22:25,688
<i>I'm told that Melon survived,
but I don't know his condition.</i>

412
00:22:27,648 --> 00:22:28,900
<i>As for Louis...</i>

413
00:22:30,443 --> 00:22:32,528
[Juno] So you and I are just done?

414
00:22:33,446 --> 00:22:34,322
I'm sorry.

415
00:22:36,407 --> 00:22:37,617
[Juno] Well, then...

416
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:40,828
...take care, Louis.

417
00:22:43,915 --> 00:22:46,000
[voice-over] <i>And as for my boy, Legoshi...</i>

418
00:22:48,961 --> 00:22:50,338
I want to be with you,

419
00:22:51,839 --> 00:22:53,466
every day for the rest of my life.

420
00:22:54,801 --> 00:22:55,676
Well...

421
00:22:56,511 --> 00:22:59,680
Is that a proposal?

422
00:23:00,306 --> 00:23:02,100
- Yes it is.
- [groans softly]

423
00:23:02,725 --> 00:23:04,685
A wolf and a rabbit...

424
00:23:04,769 --> 00:23:07,230
That won't be
the easiest of relationships.

425
00:23:07,814 --> 00:23:10,525
But we'll keep going, no matter what.

426
00:23:13,319 --> 00:23:15,905
No, don't bend over!
I can reach up to you!

427
00:23:18,741 --> 00:23:20,868
I'm falling, I'm falling! Hold me!

428
00:23:20,952 --> 00:23:22,120
Uh, Haru!

429
00:23:22,203 --> 00:23:23,496
I see you, wolf!

430
00:23:23,579 --> 00:23:24,622
Let go of her!

431
00:23:25,665 --> 00:23:27,792
[chuckles] It's alright.

432
00:23:27,875 --> 00:23:29,400
{\an8}We're together! [chuckles]
